🔐 TCP Three-Way Handshake (Easy Explanation)

Jab bhi 2 systems (client aur server) connection banate hain (jaise ESB → WhatsApp), TCP pehle ek “handshake” karta hai to confirm both sides are ready.

🔁 Step-by-Step Flow
✅ 1. SYN (Client → Server)

👉 Client bolta hai:

“Hi server, mujhe tumse connection banana hai”

📦 Packet: SYN

👉 Example:
ESB → WhatsApp
“Can I connect?”

✅ 2. SYN-ACK (Server → Client)

👉 Server reply karta hai:

“Okay, main ready hoon + I also acknowledge your request”

📦 Packet: SYN + ACK

👉 Meaning:
✔ I received your request
✔ I am also ready to connect

✅ 3. ACK (Client → Server)

👉 Client final confirm karta hai:

“Perfect, I also confirm connection is established”

📦 Packet: ACK

🎯 Final Result

After this:

✔ Connection is established
✔ Data transfer start ho sakta hai

📊 Simple Diagram
Client (ESB)        Server (WhatsApp)
     |  SYN   -------------------->
     |         <--------------------  SYN-ACK
     |  ACK   -------------------->
     | 
     | ===== CONNECTION ESTABLISHED =====
❌ Agar issue ho jaye (your case link)

If handshake breaks like:

SYN sent ✔
SYN-ACK missing ❌
or wrong ACK ❌

👉 Then:

Connection fail
Timeout
RST packet sent (reset) Proxy sends RST (Reset)

👉 Meaning: “I am aborting this connection”
💡 One-line memory trick

👉 SYN = I want to connect
👉 SYN-ACK = I accept + ready
👉 ACK = connection confirmed


