🧠 What is ESB Application?

👉 ESB = Enterprise Service Bus

💡 Simple meaning:

ESB is like a middleman system that connects different applications together.

📌 Example:

Think like this:

App A (your system)
App B (WhatsApp / CRM / billing system)

👉 Instead of connecting directly, ESB sits in between and manages communication.

🧩 What ESB does:
Sends messages between systems
Converts formats (if needed)
Routes requests to correct system
Tracks communication

👉 In short: ESB = Communication bridge between systems


🌐 What is Sky-high Proxy?

👉 Sky-high proxy is a network gateway / security middle layer

💡 Simple meaning:

It is like a security gate + traffic controller between ESB and internet.

📌 What it does:
Controls outgoing internet traffic
Applies security rules
Routes requests to external systems (like WhatsApp)
Helps in monitoring & logging

👉 In short:
Sky-high proxy = Gateway to internet with security control

🔁 Simple Flow (your case)
ESB Application
      ↓
Sky-high Proxy
      ↓
Internet
      ↓
WhatsApp / External API

