🌐 What is curl command used for?

👉 curl = Client URL

It is a command-line tool used to send and receive data from a server over the internet.

💡 Simple meaning:

👉 curl is used to check if a URL / API is working or not

📌 What it does:
✅ 1. Test API / URL response
curl https://api.whatsapp.com

👉 Checks if server is responding

✅ 2. Send request to API (GET/POST)
curl -X GET https://example.com

👉 Used to fetch data from server

✅ 3. Send data to server (POST request)
curl -X POST https://api.example.com/login -d "user=abc&pass=123"

👉 Used to send data like login, OTP, form data

✅ 4. Check HTTPS connection

👉 Useful in your ESB/WhatsApp case to verify connectivity

🧠 In your job context (very important)

You use curl to check:

✔ API is reachable or not
✔ SSL/HTTPS working or not
✔ Response is coming or timeout
