ESB Application
   (Private IP)
        ↓
Sky-high Proxy
   (Private Network + NAT)
        ↓
Airtel Public IP (NAT)
        ↓
Internet / Firewall
        ↓
WhatsApp API Server
   (Public IP: 125.17.6.13)
🔐 Key Insight (Very Important)

👉 WhatsApp NEVER sees your private IP
👉 They ONLY see your public NAT IP

So when whitelist issue happens:
✔ It is usually your NAT Public IP that must be whitelisted

💡 One-line memory trick

👉 Private IP = internal identity
👉 Public IP = internet identity (visible to WhatsApp)

